    "problem_statement": "## Problem\n\nA restaurant chain rotates menu items daily. Given a string `menu` of length `n` representing daily menu item codes (lowercase letters), and an integer `k`, find the length of the **longest substring** that contains **at most `k` distinct characters**.\n\nThis models finding the longest uninterrupted stretch of days where the total variety of items on the menu does not exceed `k` distinct types.\n\n## Function Signature\n```python\ndef longest_k_distinct(menu: str, k: int) -> int:\n```\n\n## Input / Output\n- **Input**: A string `menu` and an integer `k`\n- **Output**: Length of the longest substring with at most `k` distinct characters. Return `0` if `k == 0` or `menu` is empty.",
