        "approach": "Check all O(n^2) substrings. For each, count distinct characters using a set. Track the maximum length of those with at most k distinct characters.",
        "code": "def longest_k_distinct(menu, k):\n    if k == 0 or not menu:\n        return 0\n    n = len(menu)\n    max_len = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        seen = set()\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            seen.add(menu[j])\n            if len(seen) <= k:\n                max_len = max(max_len, j - i + 1)\n            else:\n                break  # adding more chars only increases distinct count\n    return max_len",
